<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-1.Introduction">1. Introduction</h2>
<p>The <strong>Venue Booking and Services Application (VBSA Mega)</strong> =
is a comprehensive digital platform designed to streamline the end-to-end m=
anagement of venue onboarding, project planning, audit coordination, and se=
rvice bookings for large-scale examination and event operations. It brings =
together multiple stakeholders=E2=80=94ranging from educational institution=
s and service providers to project administrators and clients=E2=80=94into =
a unified, role-based ecosystem that ensures transparency, efficiency, and =
accountability.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-2.Objective">2. Objective</h2>
<p>The primary objective of VBSA Mega is to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Digitize and automate the <strong>venue onboarding and approval process<=
/strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enable <strong>project-based planning and resource allocation</strong> a=
cross multiple venues.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Facilitate <strong>real-time coordination</strong> between clients, venu=
e owners, auditors, and service providers.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure <strong>data integrity, audit compliance</strong>, and <strong>ro=
le-based access control</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Provide a <strong>centralized dashboard</strong> for managing bookings, =
contracts, audits, and service logistics.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>This platform is built to support scalable, secure, and efficient operat=
ions for high-stakes projects such as government exams, corporate assessmen=
ts, and academic events.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-3.TargetUsers">3. Target Users</h2>
<p>VBSA Mega is designed for a diverse set of user roles, each with specifi=
c responsibilities and access privileges:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Project Head</strong>: Initiates and configures projects, define=
s timelines and slot types, and manages venue mapping, reviews audits, appr=
oves venues, and oversees project execution.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Venue Owner</strong>: Manages venue profiles, authorizes manager=
s, and handles bookings and contracts.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Venue Manager / Agent / Aggregator</strong>: Requests authorizat=
ion, submits venue details, and manages availability.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Client</strong>: Requests venue bookings, reviews contracts, and=
 manages booking statuses.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Client Agent</strong>: Acts on behalf of clients to coordinate b=
ookings and service requirements.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Service Provider</strong>: Offers manpower, logistics, and techn=
ical services linked to venue bookings.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Principal</strong>: Oversees venue readiness and ensures complia=
nce with audit and booking standards.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
