<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-D.VenueAuditor">D. Venue Auditor</h2>
<div id=3D"expander-623662946" class=3D"expand-container">
<div id=3D"expander-control-623662946" class=3D"expand-control">
<span class=3D"expand-control-icon"><img style=3D"vertical-align:middle;" c=
lass=3D"expand-control-image" src=3D"f21dae11798d2af9ea1168a5798afeb45451aa=
fce182619f3dbe43f2e8b53628" width=3D"16" height=3D"16"></span><span class=
=3D"expand-control-text">1. Venue Auditor onboarding / registration</span>
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-content-623662946" class=3D"expand-content">
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-1.Interface:.20">1. <strong>Interface</strong>:</h2>
<p>Venue Auditor =E2=80=93 Registration and Onboarding Flow</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-2.Role:.20">2. <strong>Role</strong>:</h2>
<p><strong>Venue Auditor</strong><br>
Venue Auditors are external or internal stakeholders responsible for valida=
ting and auditing the physical or functional readiness of venues before pro=
ject execution.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-3.Description:.20">3. <strong>Description</strong>:<=
/h2>
<p>This screen allows invited Venue Auditors to complete their onboarding a=
nd access the audit system. Project Heads invite auditors by entering their=
 email IDs during project creation. If an auditor is not already registered=
, they receive a verification link via email, which redirects them to a <st=
rong>pre-filled registration form</strong>.</p>
<p>This registration flow ensures that:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Only invited users can register as Venue Auditors</p></li>
<li>
<p>Auditors complete a one-time registration and secure their login credent=
ials</p></li>
<li>
<p>Access is granted post email verification and password setup</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-4.AccessPoint:.8">4. <strong>Access Point</strong>:<=
/h2>
<p>Via <strong>Email Invitation Link</strong> sent by the Project Head from=
 the Project Creation screen</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-5.FunctionalOverview:.8">5. <strong>Functional Overv=
iew</strong>:</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"3de437c5-4c90-45ff-b5b6-758=
38033ccfa" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Step</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Screen</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Description</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Register</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Auditor sees a form with their email pre-filled and locked. Other fields=
 (name, contact, location, optional company name) are filled manually.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Email Verification Prompt</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>After submitting the registration form, a prompt tells them to check ema=
il and verify using a link. Option to resend link if needed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Set Password</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Once the email is verified, the auditor is redirected to a form where th=
ey must set a password and confirm it.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Login</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Auditor can now log in using email and password created.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-6.FieldDetails:">6. <strong>Field Details</strong>:<=
/h2>
<h3 id=3D"VBSAMega:BRD-6.1.RegistrationForm:">6.1. Registration Form:</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"2fce0985-bba9-463c-9628-df0=
df21fded7" class=3D"confluenceTable">
